  "issue_number": 269,
  "issue_title": "add a BIG-Bench Hard (BBH) reasoning adapter (multiple-choice + exact-match, no code execution)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nAdd **BIG-Bench Hard (BBH)** \u2014 the 27-task suite of challenging reasoning problems \u2014 as a first-class benchmark: a `bbh.py` adapter that loads the subtasks, renders their prompts, and grades answers by the two formats BBH uses (**multiple-choice** letter and **exact-match** free-form). Pure text scoring \u2014 **no code execution, no sandbox** \u2014 so it reuses the shared answer extractors and adds no untrusted-execution surface. Default config and every existing benchmark are unchanged.\n\n## Goal / Motivation\n\nThe router's reasoning/knowledge coverage is currently only MMLU, MMLU-Pro, and GPQA  (`reward.CHOICE_BENCHMARKS`; `MmluAdapter` / `GpqaAdapter` / `MmluProAdapter`). **BBH has no adapter or loader**, so one of the most widely-reported multi-step-reasoning benchmarks can't be trained or evaluated on. BBH is valuable because its 27 subtasks (logical deduction, causal judgement, multistep arithmetic, tracking shuffled objects, word sorting, boolean expressions, \u2026) stress *routing* precisely where it matters: a good coordinator should send hard-reasoning tasks to a strong \"Thinker\". Unlike the two code adapters, BBH is graded by comparing a short textual answer to a gold target, so it needs **no runner and no isolation** \u2014 it slots cleanly into the existing `score_text`-style scoring.\n\n## Proposal\n\nA single adapter family covering the 27 subtasks, fully offline-testable (HF loader guarded with a toy fallback; scoring is pure string comparison).\n\n1. **`src/trinity/adapters/bbh.py`** \u2014 `task_type` is `MCQ` for choice subtasks and   `MATH`/free-form for exact-match subtasks:\n   - `BBHReference` \u2014 structured reference: `answer` (gold target), `answer_type`\n     (`\"multiple_choice\"` | `\"exact_match\"`), and the `choices` when multiple-choice,\n     with `to_dict`/`from_dict`/`is_valid`.\n   - `SUBTASKS` \u2014 the 27 BBH subtask names with their answer types (choice vs exact).\n   - `load_bbh_tasks(subtask, split, max_items, seed)` \u2014 lazy/guarded HuggingFace loader\n     (`lukaemon/bbh` / `maveriq/bigbenchhard`, per-subtask config) with an offline toy\n     fallback; normalized `Task`s carrying the subtask + answer type in `task.meta`.\n   - `build_bbh_prompt()` \u2014 the BBH question format with an explicit \"final answer\"\n     instruction so the answer is parseable.\n   - `score_bbh(candidate, reference)` \u2014 dispatch on `answer_type`: reuse\n     `reward.extract_choice_letter` for multiple-choice, and a normalized exact-match\n     (case/space/punctuation-folded, `Yes/No/True/False`, integers) for the rest.\n   - `BBHAdapter` \u2014 `load_tasks` / `build_prompt` / `score_output` (no `runner`; this\n     benchmark never executes code).\n2. **Registry + tables** \u2014 register `bbh` (and per-subtask aliases like `bbh_boolean_expressions`\n   if useful); add the name(s) to the appropriate `reward` benchmark tables so\n   `score_text`/`has_answer` recognise them.\n3. **Tests** \u2014 `tests/test_bbh_adapter.py`: schema round-trip; guarded loader + toy\n   fallback for both a multiple-choice subtask and an exact-match subtask; prompt shape;\n   and scoring \u2014 a correct MC letter and a correct free-form answer score `1.0`, wrong\n   ones `0.0`, robust to phrasing (\"the answer is (B)\", \"Answer: valid\", trailing\n   punctuation). Torch-free, offline.\n\nExpected size \u2248 400\u2013550 lines across adapter + tests, in line with the merged MMLU-Pro (#43) and SWE-bench (#42) adapters.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] `get_adapter(\"bbh\").load_tasks(...)` returns normalized `Task`s; `available_adapters()`\n      includes it.\n- [ ] `from_dict(to_dict(x)) == x`; a reference missing its gold answer is `is_valid() == False`.\n- [ ] Multiple-choice subtasks grade via letter extraction; exact-match subtasks grade via\n      normalized string equality \u2014 a correct answer scores `1.0`, a wrong one `0.0`.\n- [ ] Offline: no network, no GPU, no torch import from the adapter or its tests; **no\n      subprocess / code execution anywhere** (this is a text benchmark).\n- [ ] `pytest tests/`, `ruff check src/`, `mypy src/` stay green.\n\n## Impact\n\nAdds a standard, high-signal multi-step-reasoning benchmark to the routing competition, broadening coverage beyond knowledge-recall MCQ (MMLU/GPQA) into the reasoning regime where routing to a strong Thinker pays off \u2014 with **zero execution surface** (no sandbox to review) and no change to existing benchmarks or the frozen protocol.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-14T18:38:31.000Z",
